From 28f1e2608eff31774829a3c88acdaad8493b17cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Dannapel <ian.dannapel@iris-sensing.com>
Date: Fri, 5 Jun 2026 09:19:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 03/29] misc: iris: add DSP DMA-BUF address helper

Add /dev/irma_dsp_addr for Gen6 userspace that passes DMA-BUF backed capture buffers to the SHARC cores.
The helper pins DMA-BUF file descriptors, validates offsets against the DSP memory window and returns DSP-visible addresses through a small ioctl ABI.

Signed-off-by: Ian Dannapel <ian.dannapel@iris-sensing.com>
---
 drivers/misc/iris/Kconfig          |  14 ++
 drivers/misc/iris/Makefile         |   3 +
 drivers/misc/iris/irma-dsp-addr.c  | 353 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 include/uapi/linux/irma-dsp-addr.h |  59 +++++
 4 files changed, 429 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/misc/iris/Kconfig
 create mode 100644 drivers/misc/iris/Makefile
 create mode 100644 drivers/misc/iris/irma-dsp-addr.c
 create mode 100644 include/uapi/linux/irma-dsp-addr.h

